WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.800
Get ready for a fast and furious dose of summer
action.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.760
Reviews are racing in for Hobbs &amp; Shaw, a
standalone spinoff presented by the Fast and

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.640
Furious franchise.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.679
It's generally agreed that the film delivers
exactly what it promises: plenty of high-octane,

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:19.110
over-the-top set pieces, held together by
lots of witty banter and some serious chemistry

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.460
between its two leads.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.280
"No way, this guy's a real a------"

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:29.320
With 102 reviews counted, the film currently
stands at a 72% average on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.680
Hobbs &amp; Shaw finds our titular duo teaming
up to eradicate a serious threat: Brixton

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.010
Lore, portrayed by Idris Elba, is a superpowered
terrorist and self-proclaimed "black Superman"

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.460
intent on unleashing a potent virus on the
world.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.000
"Who the hell are you?"

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:45.740
"Bad guy."

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.280
Back in January, star Dwayne Johnson promised
that

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.280
"[The film will be] the biggest showdown the
FAST &amp; FURIOUS franchise has ever seen"

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.400
Well, it certainly has the right pedigree.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.290
It was penned by Chris Morgan, the screenwriter
behind The Fast and the Furious: Tokyo Drift,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:07.380
Fast &amp; Furious, Fast Five, Fast &amp; Furious
6, Furious 7, and The Fate of the Furious.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.860
Suffice to say, this man knows exactly what
fans want.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.760
Meanwhile, director David Leitch is a co-director
of the action-packed original John Wick, and

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.480
also delivered a similarly off-kilter blast
of craziness with last year's Deadpool 2.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.520
According to critics, Leitch and company have
delivered an exciting, entertaining action

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.760
film that takes full advantage of the crackling
chemistry between Johnson and co-star Jason

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.620
Statham.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.920
They also praised the performances by Vanessa
Kirby and Elba.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.920
On the other hand, the film's detractors focused
on the outlandish action sequences…but what

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.880
did they expect?

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:51.020
Entertainment Weekly's Leah Greenblatt understands
that the bonkers action is exactly the point,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:51.920
writing that,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.000
"[Hobbs &amp; Shaw is] a testosterone motherlode
so relentlessly, ridiculously adrenalized,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.020
it doesn't so much unfold as steadily defibrillate
you...Bodies crumple; metal clangs; and anything

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:07.310
that doesn't get punched or shot or stabbed
on sight just stands by patiently, waiting

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.180
to explode.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.580
When it's not all completely brain-numbing,
it's actually pretty fun."

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:16.700
It sounds like Brian Tallerico of RogerEbert.com
was perfectly content letting the film's kinetic

00:02:16.709 --> 00:02:18.200
energy wash over him:

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.980
"What are audiences really here for?

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.360
They want some banter between stars Jason
Statham and Dwayne Johnson?

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:23.920
Check.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.000
They want them to beat each other up a few
times?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.660
Check.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.280
A physics-defying car chase or two would be
nice?

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.280
Check and check."

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.379
Elsewhere in his review, Tallerico claimed,

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.820
"The truth is that the Summer of 2019 has
been ridiculously thin when it comes to mindless

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:37.380
fun.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.180
And there's something to be said for merely
bouncing four movie stars as charismatic as

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.450
this film's quartet off each other for just
over two hours."

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:48.480
Cleveland Plain Dealer's Chuck Yarborough
was clearly a fan of the film, effusively

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.200
gushing that,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.700
"[Hobbs &amp; Shaw is] one of the most entertaining
action movies you'll see this year...What

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:57.840
makes this film work is the humor that pours
from Johnson, and what he’s able to elicit

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.280
from his fellow actors.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.200
Particularly good are the insults in what
we used to call the 'slip fights' between

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.220
him and Statham."

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.700
Of course, plenty of critics walked away from
the film with a sour face, and there's no

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:09.810
shortage of snarky reviews out there.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.190
Donald Clarke of the Irish Times sniped,

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:16.340
"After just half an hour, I was tempted to
spread foam across the screen and scrape off

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:20.220
the stubble that was already breaking through...The
awful banter is something else.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.740
Neither man has, to be fair, much to work
with."

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.240
Jake Wilson of The Age unleashed plenty of
scorn on Morgan's screenplay and its plethora

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.000
of quips:

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.660
"The action regularly grinds to a halt so
[Hobbs and Shaw] can trade elaborate putdowns,

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:37.090
which give every sign of having been crafted
by writers whose practical experience of brawling

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.840
has occurred mostly on Twitter."

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:43.400
Keenly demonstrating how to effectively put
someone down, Wilson goes on say,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.580
"For the leading men, everything appears to
be business as usual - which hardly needs

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.029
saying in the case of Statham, a cook who
knows just one dish."

00:03:51.029 --> 00:03:55.220
Nevertheless, most critics were more than
willing to accept the film on its own terms.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:59.180
Candice Frederick of The Wrap embraced the
absurdity of the blockbuster, writing that,

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:03.620
"[The film is] very cognizant of what it is,
which is also in line with what “Fast &amp; Furious”

00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:08.469
has always been: an opportunity for alpha
men (and women) to exchange insults then eventually

00:04:08.469 --> 00:04:11.240
hug it out for the sake of some good old-fashioned
whoop-ass."

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.940
So that's what the critics had to say…now
it's time to make up your own mind.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.780
Fast &amp; Furious Presents: Hobbs &amp; Shaw opens
on August 2nd…and we're expecting to be

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.640
electrified.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.660
"Three shocks will kill a man."

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.740
"Here we go, it's a bad guy speech!"

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.640
"You had to open your big mouth, didn't ya,
huh?"

